[For "white"]
[Kind "gambit"]
[Start "london-englund 2.dxe5"]
[Name "The Englund: 2...f6"]

2... f6 { Black wants to take back on e5 and open the f-file. }
3. Nf3 { Defends the pawn and develops, which is stronger than taking on f6. If Black takes on e5, the knight takes back and stands in the centre. }
3... fxe5
4. Nxe5 { White is a clean pawn up with a knight in the middle of the board, and Black's kingside is loose. } *
